            "- The initial velocity state is projected onto the cylindrical velocity constraints before stepping; without that compatibility repair, the h-sweep measured a false low-order branch.",
            "- A post-step least-squares velocity projection closes endpoint cylindrical velocity constraints to roundoff in the baseline path. The endpoint projection audit quantifies the raw velocity residual and correction-size orders, and the endpoint KKT closure path moves the velocity correction into a square residual.",
